 "notes": [
  "The Middle Eastern Languages and Cultures (MELC) major offers two Specializations:\n- Middle Eastern Worlds\n- Middle Eastern Languages and Literature\nStudents in the Middle Eastern Languages and Literature specialization may choose an emphasis in Arabic, Hebrew, or Persian. Students in the Middle Eastern Worlds specialization may choose an emphasis in Ancient Middle Eastern Worlds or Modern Middle Eastern Worlds.\nStudents are encouraged to begin the study of a language early in their academic studies. MELC 10 (Middle Eastern Worlds: Ancient Egypt and Mesopotamia) and MELC 11 ( The Modern Middle Eastern Worlds) are required courses for the major."
 ],
